Okay, so now I know that 2.2 and 2.3 are sucky versions. I have
checked and 3.1.3 is the first version where you don't lose the
spellbook after reading it. I have tried the newer versions
occasionally, but they just lack the nostalgia factor, and they are
too complicated. I don't want to have to worry about alignments and
luck and deities and blah blah blah - just give me a nice sharp Katana
and a fireball spell and a room full of Orcs, not (gasp) multi-colored
monsters.

Honestly I think one of the things that really kills the joy for me in
the new versions is having to kick in doors all the time. If they'd
just get rid of that bloody "The Door resists!" with all the other
things going on, why do I have to try opening a door multiple times?
And to top it off they put an exclamation mark on it, as if this is
headline news. "This old dungeon door is a little stuck!!!! OMG! Wait,
let me write this in my diary!"

Here's how I think it should work: doors should have three states:
open, closed and locked. If a door is open, anything can move through
it. If it is closed, intelligent creatures can move through it but it
is assumed that they are all polite and close it after themselves. If
it is locked, then you need to unlock it or smash it in.

Seriously, why should I have to spend half my time dealing with
frickin' doorknobs? None of that nonsense in Nethack 1.4f - just
charge into the room and get on with the looting and slaying!

But since 3.4.3 seems to be four years old now, is anyone still
developing it? or is that just a copyright date? Change that door
nonsense and maybe I'll think about it.

Oh - another pet peeve - Samurai is my favourite character class but
suddenly I have to figure out what a gunyoki is and a wakazushi and a
shikizumi and a kitinabe - WTF? is there an option to keep the regular
names for things?

And newts and grid bugs? give me a frickin' break. Orcs, goblins and
zombies, those are real dungeon monsters. Seriously, who fights a
newt? Wouldn't you long sword get dull whacking at the ground trying
to hit it?

/rant

I just finished a game with my best character ever - a +7 blessed
katana, all my armor (crystal plate, elven cloak, shield, gloves,
helmets) was +4, I had 20 or so spells and was headed home with the
amulet and 58 emeralds and $35,000. STR was 18/** and I couldn't carry
any more loot. I had a wand of wishing too but there was nothing left
to wish for - I guess that wouldn't happen in NH 3.4.3. Anyhow, my
best character ever - was killing even pretty high-level monsters with
a single blow.



